Explanation of the root cause and fix:

- **Root cause**: The original audit used  
    ```js
    manifest.short_name.value || manifest.name.value || ''
    ```  
  which meant that if `short_name` was missing (or empty) it fell back to `name` (or the empty string), causing the check to fire even though no `short_name` was present.
- **Fix**: We now only apply the 12-char truncation check when `short_name` actually exists. If no `short_name` is supplied, we mark the audit as passing (`rawValue: true`) so that the missing-field audit can surface the absence of `short_name` separately.
